    "section_faq_ciHP4y": {
      "type": "section-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "text_w3qRH7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What Kites are Easiest to Fly?",
            "content": "<p>We typically recommend single-line deltas, diamonds, and parafoils for beginners. </p><p>For more in-depth advice please check out our <a href=\"https://store.kittyhawk.com/blogs/recent-articles/the-best-kites-for-beginners\" title=\"https://store.kittyhawk.com/blogs/recent-articles/the-best-kites-for-beginners\">blog post</a> on this subject!</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_GkQLky": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do All Kites Come Ready to Fly?",
            "content": "<p>No, not all kites come ready to fly.</p><p>Ready to fly means that your kite includes line and handles.</p><p>All products will say in the product description whether or not kite line is included with that kite. </p><p>If you have any questions or concerns about kite line please reach out to orders@kittyhawk.com</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_FVgRq3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What Kind of Line do I need?",
            "content": "<p>Most all of our kites come with a small amount of basic line, but it's generally not very strong so if you are flying in higher winds or open areas like the beach, we recommend you pick up some spare line. Most kites under 6ft wingspan will be fine with 50lb, 500ft line like our <a href=\"https://store.kittyhawk.com/collections/kite-line/products/50-lb-x-300-foot-kite-line-stake-winder\">stake winders</a>. (Most kites only come with maybe 25lb test 150ft)</p><p><strong>Most all of our larger kites do not come with string</strong>. Kites 9ft to about 10ft are generally good on 90lb test like our <a href=\"https://store.kittyhawk.com/collections/kite-line/products/80lb-500-ft-kite-line-yo-yo-winder\" title=\"80lb kite line\">80lb by 500ft yoyo winder</a>. But keep in mind big kites pull so if you worry you can always increase the lb test of line used to 150lb.</p><p>Big kites over 10ft to about 15ft can be flown on <a href=\"https://store.kittyhawk.com/collections/kite-line/products/150-x-500-ft-line-on-yoyo-546-0007\" title=\"150lb kite line\">150lb by 500ft line</a>. These kites will pull a good deal so wear gloves and consider your windspeed as you can upgrade to 250lb test line for caution.</p><p>Big kites from about 16ft to 19ft should be flown with caution. These kites should be securely anchored before launching and at least <a href=\"https://store.kittyhawk.com/products/250lb-line-on-yoyo-146631\" title=\"250lb test line\">250lb test line</a> used.</p><p>Show Kites, Sleds and large ultrafoils are massive and should never be flown alone, should always be anchored before flying and gloves should be worn. Kites that are 19ft generally fly with <a href=\"https://store.kittyhawk.com/products/500-500-yo-yo-winder-115078\" title=\"500lb test kite line\">500lb test kite line</a> and kites bigger than that can use anywhere from 800lb to 1,500lb kite line</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_rf9CFH": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How Windy Does it Need to Be?",
            "content": "<p>Each kite is designed to excel in different wind conditions. Please check the product description for the correct wind range for your kite. Also check out our blog post on getting the best kite flying experience <a href=\"https://store.kittyhawk.com/blogs/recent-articles/how-to-improve-your-kite-flying-experience\" title=\"https://store.kittyhawk.com/blogs/recent-articles/how-to-improve-your-kite-flying-experience\">here</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_EfPncz": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Where Can I Fly my Kite?",
            "content": "<p>The best places to fly a kite are large open areas away from trees and power lines with plenty of space to avoid other people.</p><p>Check out our <a href=\"https://store.kittyhawk.com/blogs/recent-articles/professional-kite-flyers-guide-to-the-obx\" title=\"https://store.kittyhawk.com/blogs/recent-articles/professional-kite-flyers-guide-to-the-obx\">blog post</a> on best places to fly when your in the Outer Banks!</p>"
          }
        }
      },
